INT. DAIRY-CASE AISLE, 24-HOUR GROCERY - 3 A.M.

Fluorescent hum. Forty brands of yogurt, all the same.

TOBIAS WREN-ALDRIDGE (30s, Regional Synergy Lead, lanyard, no pulse) holds a laser pointer at a shelf.

TOBIAS
Team. Our learning: yogurt is a journey.

Four night-shift stockers stare back.

PRISCILLA OYELARAN (40s, forklift certified, unimpressed) holds a pallet jack like a shield.

DMITRI "DIMA" ROSENFELD (20s, hoodie, headphones around his neck) eats a yogurt, deliberately.

HYACINTH PELL (50s, reading glasses on a chain, ex-accountant) checks her watch.

MARGUERITE (60s, no last name anyone remembers) is asleep standing up.

TOBIAS (CONT'D)
Going forward, we are removing the word "expired."

PRISCILLA
We're what?

TOBIAS
We're reframing it as "mature."

Dima's spoon stops. He puts it down.

DIMA
That's illegal.

TOBIAS
That's agile.

HYACINTH
(to no one)
I left a pension for this.

Tobias fires the laser pointer at Marguerite's forehead.

MARGUERITE
(eyes closed)
Is it the fire?

PRISCILLA
No, Marguerite. It's the Synergy Lead.

Marguerite nods, drifts off again. Tobias lowers the pointer.

TOBIAS
Okay. Okay. Is there anything anyone wants to say before we align?

Silence. Dima raises his yogurt like a toast.

DIMA
Mature.
